Title: I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT A SPEC WAS
Author: vibecode-blog pipeline
Contact: @lazy_genius2025

== act: hook ==

INT. REMOTE BEACH - DAY

A CLAY CHARACTER sits on a beach chair with a single laptop. Behind him, three holographic monitors glow, showing real-time sync across three distant DESKTOP MACHINES.

NARRATOR
(cool, nonchalant)
My three computers finally act like one. I can work from anywhere.

The character taps a key. All three holographic screens pulse in perfect unison.

NARRATOR
(cynical)
But getting here? It took six months of absolute hell.

== act: fury ==

INT. DARK OFFICE - NIGHT

The character is illuminated only by the red glow of a "SYSTEM CRASH" error on his monitor. He looks sleep-deprived, staring at a mountain of messy clay wires.

NARRATOR
(pissed)
Monday morning. Everything stopped. Ten thousand lines of code, and half of it was garbage.

CLOSE UP - MONITOR

A jagged crack opens in the screen, revealing a door handle labeled "SHELL INJECTION".

NARRATOR
(raw)
AI wrote a back door. I approved it. I didn't even know it was there.

== act: mess ==

INT. THE CODE JUNGLE - DAY

The character is hacking through a forest of tangled, duplicating clay vines. Five identical STUBBY ROBOTS are building the same wooden bridge in five different, conflicting ways.

NARRATOR
(manic)
Five agents building the same thing. Three date formatters. Four ways to validate a string.

The character tries to pull one vine, and the entire forest collapses on him.

NARRATOR
(cynical)
It looked convincing. That's why it was dangerous. I was vibe coding with no map.

== act: insight ==

INT. CLEAN STUDIO - DAY

The character is pinning a simple, four-line note to a pristine off-white wall. The note is a simple blueprint of a bridge.

NARRATOR
(resolute)
Implementation is free. But deciding what to build? That's the only thing that isn't.

WIDE SHOT

The character walks across a now-sturdy, simple bridge. The messy jungle is gone.

NARRATOR
(philosopher)
Specs don't come from conference rooms. They come from the grind.
